  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Exponential growth and its inverse, the logarithm, appear throughout the mathematics section.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Exp & logs",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( \\log_b x=y \\) means \\( b^{y}=x \\); \\( \\log(xy)=\\log x+\\log y \\); \\( \\log(x^{n})=n\\log x \\); \\( \\ln e=1 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Definition",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( b^{y}=x \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\log x+\\log y \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Power",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( n\\log x \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Natural",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\ln e=1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Evaluate \\( \\log_2 16 \\). \\[ 2^{4}=16\\Rightarrow 4. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve for \\(x\\): \\(\\log_2(x+3)+\\log_2(x-1)=5.\\) <details><summary>Show solution</summary><div>Combine: \\(\\log_2[(x+3)(x-1)]=5\\Rightarrow(x+3)(x-1)=32.\\) \\(x^2+2x-3=32\\Rightarrow x^2+2x-35=0\\Rightarrow(x+7)(x-5)=0.\\) Reject \\(x=-7\\) (makes \\(x-1=-8<0\\)). <strong>\\(x=5.\\)</strong></div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
